Subject: [PATCH] fix(instagram,messenger): accept ig_reel and degrade unknown attachment types

Minimal cherry-pick of the attachmentTypeSchema hunk from upstream 4caf7e8 (PR #1053),
applied on top of 064ff2d305c6e76404562db372ee40bce75aae8e.

Nothing else from that PR is included: no private-reply feature, no is_deleted, no
reply_to.story, no referral/postback changes, no reaction schema.

Rationale: on the base revision, an Instagram DM carrying attachments[].type = "ig_reel"
fails schema validation, and the handler does `return void` on failure — discarding the
entire webhook POST. Because Meta batches multiple messaging events per POST, one
unrecognised type drops every message in that batch, including unrelated text messages.

diff --git a/integrations/instagram/src/schemas.ts b/integrations/instagram/src/schemas.ts
--- a/integrations/instagram/src/schemas.ts
+++ b/integrations/instagram/src/schemas.ts
@@ -28,16 +28,22 @@ export type InstagramActions = {
 }

 // Common attachment types — includes all types Instagram may send in a webhook
-const attachmentTypeSchema = z.enum([
-  "image",
-  "video",
-  "audio",
-  "file",
-  "sticker",
-  "location",
-  "share",
-  "fallback",
-])
+const attachmentTypeSchema = z
+  .enum([
+    "image",
+    "video",
+    "audio",
+    "file",
+    "sticker",
+    "location",
+    "share",
+    "fallback",
+    "story_mention",
+    "ig_reel",
+    "reel",
+    "template",
+  ])
+  .catch("fallback")

 // Base attachment payload — url optional because location/share have no url
 const baseAttachmentPayloadSchema = z.object({
